{% comment %}
The decider's questions for confirming numbers (BuildGoal/Start.goal ConfirmNumbers): one yes/no per number a step's
code writes that its words don't write as digits, under the number's id (goal.step.unwritten Id). A no refuses the
number as invented; the check that found it reads no human language — the decider does the reading.
The eval's shape (tools/decider/prompt_c.py confirm_questions); keep the two equal.
Needs: numbers (the UnwrittenNumber error's Details.numbers).
{% endcomment %}
{
{%- assign sep = "" -%}
{%- for n in numbers -%}
{%- capture ask %}Step {{ n.Step }} is `{{ n.Text }}`. Its code writes {{ n.Action }}({{ n.Property }}={{ n.Value }}). Does step {{ n.Step }} give {{ n.Property }} the value {{ n.Value }}?{% endcapture %}
{{ sep }}
  {{ n.Id | json }}: {
    "type": "noul",
    "instructions": {{ ask | json }},
    "criteria": {"true": "the step's words give that value, in any wording or language", "false": "the step's words don't give it: the value is invented"}
  }
{%- assign sep = "," -%}
{%- endfor %}
}
